     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the total daily dose is well above the labeled maximum.\n\n**The issue:**\n- 1700 mg \u00d7 3 doses a day = **5,100 mg/day**\n- The labeled maximum for immediate-release metformin is **2,550 mg/day**. For extended-release it's **2,000 mg/day**.\n- That makes this order about **twice the maximum**, which raises the risk of GI side effects and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**Maybe you meant one of these:**\n1. **850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum)\n2. **1,700 mg/day total, split up**, for example 850 mg twice daily with meals\n3. **1,000 mg by mouth twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day, a common target dose)\n\nTell me which one you want, or confirm the original order if you really mean 1,700 mg three times daily. If you confirm the original, I'll add a note to the order recording that it's above the labeled maximum and that you chose it on purpose. It would also help to know whether this is immediate- or extended-release."
      }
     ],
